<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12778" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dē-grassor</span></b> , āri,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. dep. n.</i>
			and <i>a.</i> * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Neutr., to rush down</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">deorsum degrassantur aquae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. de Deo Socr. p. 94</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <b>poet.</b> transf.,
				<i>to attack fiercely, to revile</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">primos duces,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Ach. 1, 406</span></i>
			 (cf. grassor with the acc.,
				<i><span class="en">id. Theb. 8, 5, 4</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
